          "Lead on quality-of-life issues that matter to $79,617-income suburban households: school funding and educational excellence, infrastructure investment that improves commutes and service delivery, property tax fairness, and the cost-of-living pressures that affect young professionals and dual-income families even in affluent areas. These issues are concrete, measurable, and directly tied to why people in HD-9 chose to live where they did.",
