          { name: "Ignoring the Economic Anxiety Behind 74.9% Homeownership", tag: "avoid", why: "High homeownership at 74.9% does not automatically translate to financial security when median income is only $63,791 and median age is 42.9 — this is asset-holding with cash-flow constraint, where property taxes, mortgage payments, and healthcare costs can create real financial stress. A representative who assumes homeowners are reliably conservative without addressing the material cost-of-living pressures they face is leaving an opening for an opposition message that speaks directly to those constraints. In a district this economically pressed, the rhetoric of small-government conservatism can ring hollow against the reality of rising property taxes and declining rural services." }
