          "Address the college-attainment gap as a workforce-development priority: at 26.7% college-educated adults, significantly below state and national averages, the district faces a youth economic-mobility constraint that requires specific legislative attention to workforce training, community college funding, and rural job creation — not generic conservative positioning.",
