          "Lead with working-class economic security: address healthcare costs, housing affordability, and childcare access as specific legislative priorities for a constituency that is solidly Republican but materially stressed on daily cost-of-living. Generic conservative positioning will not hold a renter-substantial (24.7%) district against an opponent offering concrete answers on these issues.",
          "Build distinct engagement tracks for renters and homeowners: the 24.7% renter minority has different economic stakes than the 75% homeowner majority, and both need to see the representative speaking to their specific concerns rather than defaulting entirely to homeowner-centric messaging around property taxes and school choice.",
