          { name: "Positioning the Incumbent as Disconnected from Young, Working-Class Concerns", tag: "avoid", why: "Any opposition messaging that characterizes the incumbent as indifferent to renter households' struggle with housing costs, Hispanic/Latino workers' wage stagnation, or young adults' healthcare access risks being heard by the district's actual majority as accurate observation rather than partisan attack. The demographic profile is specific and measurable: 53.2% renters, 31.8 median age, 20.4% college attainment, $63,664 income. If the incumbent's legislative record or public positioning can be credibly linked to policies that worsen these constituencies' material conditions — opposing tenant protections, supporting healthcare cost increases, or blocking education funding — that becomes a structural vulnerability, not a messaging opportunity." }
