          "Engage each of the district's racial and ethnic communities with specific constituent attention: the diversity of GA-HD-35 (53% white, 23.51% Black, 13.72% Hispanic, 4.02% Asian) means that a generic urban progressive message can obscure distinct needs around economic mobility, small business access, and community safety that vary by neighborhood and community; service-focused governance that listens and responds to each community's priorities is the foundation for holding 61% and building toward 65%+.",
          "Address the 39% Republican opposition directly: in an educated, younger urban district, Republican voters are not cultural conservatives but likely fiscal conservatives or quality-of-service skeptics; acknowledge their concerns about government efficiency and results delivery rather than dismissing them as partisan opponents, and demonstrate that Democratic governance is delivering fiscal responsibility and real results on the problems residents face.",
          "Prioritize transit, walkability, and neighborhood service delivery: the 32.5-year median age and high renter rate describe a constituency that depends on public transit, values neighborhood walkability, and evaluates elected officials on whether basic services work; pot-hole response times, transit reliability, park maintenance, and public safety matter more in this district than abstract policy positioning, and visible attention to these fundamentals is the foundation for Democratic durability."
