          { name: "Healthcare Affordability & Access", tag: "lean-into", why: "At $148,563 median income, this is an affluent constituency, but healthcare costs for families with multiple members and aging parents create real financial constraints even at this income level. Insurance market competition, prescription drug cost management, local hospital capacity and emergency services, and the viability of primary care in suburban networks are the material healthcare concerns for a professional-class constituency. A legislative agenda that addresses healthcare affordability through market competition, regulatory efficiency, and local provider capacity demonstrates governance competence that resonates with economically sophisticated voters who understand healthcare as both a personal necessity and a fiscal sustainability question." },
          { name: "Asian American Community Engagement & Policy Specificity", tag: "careful", why: "At 16.11% of the district — one in six constituents — the Asian American population is large enough to be outcome-determinative in a competitive race and educated, professional, and economically integrated in ways that make them swing voters rather than a locked-in partisan base. Asian American professionals have voted Republican historically on economic grounds, but increasingly evaluate on specific policy execution: education attainment pathways, healthcare access, small business regulatory environment, and immigration policy that treats their communities with precision rather than generic 'minority outreach' framing. Any candidate who engages this community with genuine policy specificity on their material concerns builds a durable coalition; any candidate who offers catchall minority rhetoric will find this educated, sophisticated constituency open to Democratic alternatives." },
          { name: "Treating 62% as a Safe Majority", tag: "avoid", why: "A 62-38 result in a district with 72.7% college education, $148,563 income, and a professional-class demographic composition is not a safe Republican majority — it is a plurality held by alignment between the incumbent's governance record and the expectations of an educationally sophisticated, economically mobile constituency that evaluates on competence rather than partisan inheritance. The 38% Democratic share in an affluent, educated suburban district is a structural vulnerability signal: any candidate who campaigns as though 62% represents a durable floor rather than a margin that requires active demonstration of governing quality will lose ground to Democratic alternatives credibly positioned on competence and constituent service." },
          { name: "Ideological Positioning Over Constituent Service Messaging", tag: "avoid", why: "HD-47's constituency is economically sophisticated and educated to the point where abstract conservative positioning on cultural or ideological questions is less persuasive than concrete evidence that government is delivering material improvements to their quality of life — education, healthcare, transportation, property tax fairness. Any candidate who leads messaging with partisan conflict, cultural positioning, or ideology-first framing rather than with specific legislative accomplishments on the issues that affect household economics and daily life will be perceived as out of step with a constituency that prioritizes competence over ideology. This is a district where 'we delivered better schools and lower healthcare costs' beats 'we fought the culture war' in electoral weight." }
