          "Engage the Asian American community as a distinct constituency with professional and policy specificity: education attainment, healthcare access, small business regulatory environment, and immigration policy precision matter to this 16% of the district; any candidate who treats Asian American voters as a generic 'minority' bloc rather than a high-skill professional population will cede the opportunity to Democratic competitors offering more sophisticated engagement.",
          "Recognize that 38% opposition in an affluent, educated district is not a minority faction — it is evidence that swing voters in this constituency are evaluating on competence and constituent service, not inherited Republican affiliation; any candidate who treats the seat as safe rather than as requiring active demonstration of governance quality will be vulnerable to a credible Democratic challenger offering better execution."
