          "Lead with healthcare cost and access for affluent families: at $157,902 income with 73.1% college education, this is a constituency of employed professionals with healthcare stakes in both insurance affordability and quality care access — a 60-40 margin suggests the incumbent may not be addressing this constituency's healthcare concerns with adequate specificity.",
          "Engage the 20% Asian and Hispanic professional population as a distinct constituent group: these are not immigrant communities requiring integration messaging, but affluent suburban professionals whose economic interests align with the district's overall profile yet whose civic and political expectations may differ from the white majority on representation, workplace equity, and immigration policy.",
          "Recognize that 60% in an affluent suburban Georgia district is not a safe majority: college-educated suburban voters have demonstrated capacity to swing toward Democrats on specific policy issues and candidate quality; consolidating existing support without active engagement of the 40% opposition and identification of specific policy gaps leaves this seat more competitive than the margin suggests."
