          { name: "Housing Affordability & Renter Constituency Engagement", tag: "lean-into", why: "At 48% renters, GA-HD-60 has a substantial constituency managing housing costs in an expensive urban market—younger professionals building wealth, families stretching budgets, and fixed-income seniors all occupy the same geography and share concerns about displacement pressure and affordability. Rental housing policy, zoning reform, property tax fairness, and anti-displacement initiatives are concrete governance areas where a legislator can demonstrate active engagement with the material economic concerns of nearly half the district's households." },
          { name: "Accountability to Black Professional & Business Communities", tag: "careful", why: "The 63% Black majority includes professionals, entrepreneurs, and civic leaders who are embedded in the district's economic and social infrastructure and whose satisfaction is the core of the 72% Democratic margin. Black-owned businesses, professional networks, and community institutions are organized constituencies with capacity to withdraw support or mobilize alternatives if they conclude the representative is not genuinely serving their interests. Regular, substantive engagement with these communities—not token acknowledgment—is essential to durability of the margin." },
          { name: "Treating 72% as a Safe Electoral Floor", tag: "avoid", why: "The 72% result reflects current performance and constituent satisfaction, not permanent Democratic lock in an educated, organized urban constituency with demonstrated capacity to evaluate alternatives. Any incumbent who treats the margin as a given and deprioritizes constituent service, governance delivery, and community accountability will find that assumption tested when an organized challenger emerges. This is a seat held through active performance, not inherited voter alignment." },
          { name: "Neglecting Younger Professional Constituency Economic Concerns", tag: "avoid", why: "The 35-year median age and 51% college education rate indicate a professional constituency heavily weighted toward younger adults establishing careers, managing student debt, and evaluating whether they can build wealth in Atlanta's expensive housing market. Abstract ideological positioning without specific attention to student debt relief, housing affordability, healthcare costs, and economic opportunity will alienate a constituency that is deeply engaged in evaluating whether government is reducing friction in their economic lives." }
