          { name: "Young Adult Credential and Wage Access", tag: "careful", why: "The 33.5-year median age combined with 21.0% college attainment means the district's younger adults are disproportionately working without bachelor's degrees in a credential-driven economy, facing wage constraints and limited advancement pathways. Workforce development, apprenticeship partnerships, industry certification programs, and policies that expand non-degree pathways to economic mobility are both material constituent needs and potential differentiators if the incumbent's opponent positions herself as more focused on young adult opportunity than the current representative has demonstrated." },
          { name: "Treating an Unopposed Victory as Substantive Validation", tag: "avoid", why: "A 100% result with no opposition is an electoral fact, not a constituent mandate or evidence of durable popularity. Unopposed victories often mask latent discontent among working-class renters, young adults without credentials, immigrant communities, and other cohorts who may not field a challenger simply because no viable alternative has emerged. An incumbent who treats the unopposed result as evidence that she is effectively serving all of HD-76's demographic constituencies will be strategically blindsided if a credible challenger enters the race and mobilizes renters or young adults around specific unmet needs." },
          { name: "Assuming Black Electoral Majority Consolidation Is Sufficient for Long-Term Holding", tag: "avoid", why: "While the 61.92% Black population is the electoral foundation of Democratic control in HD-76, relying on that plurality alone as a long-term strategy ignores the 25.99% non-Black population who could be mobilized by a challenger perceived as more responsive to Hispanic, Asian, or other community-specific needs. Coalition-building that actively demonstrates service to renters, young adults, and immigrant communities strengthens the incumbent's position; assuming the Black majority is automatically loyal regardless of service performance is the fastest pathway to a vulnerable seat." }
