          "Lead with working-class economic security: $59,382 median income with 37.1% renters means housing costs are the primary financial pressure for a substantial portion of the district; make housing affordability, renter protections, and wage growth the centerpiece of legislative focus rather than assuming economic issues are secondary to other concerns.",
          "Serve the Hispanic (16.05%) and Asian (9.94%) communities with specific legislative and constituent-service attention: these are growth constituencies in the district whose economic mobility, healthcare access, language services, and immigration-status concerns require targeted responsiveness, not absorption into a generic minority-community narrative.",
          "Engage young adults (33.5 median age) on economic opportunity and credential accessibility: without college credentials (79% of the district), younger constituents face wage constraints and limited advancement; legislative priorities around workforce development, apprenticeships, and industry partnerships demonstrate that the incumbent understands the economic reality of her actual constituency."
