          "Do not treat the unopposed status as permission for inattention: in a working-class majority-Black district, the deepest electoral risk is not general-election opposition but primary challenge from someone claiming better delivery on economic issues—and that risk grows if the incumbent is perceived as resting on partisan alignment rather than actively serving constituents' material needs."
