          { name: "Treating the District as a Reliable Vote Supply", tag: "avoid", why: "The combination of 63% Black voters, unopposed 2024 victory, and reliable Democratic margins can create an implicit assumption that the seat is 'owned' and that constituent attention is optional. This framing is strategically dangerous: Democratic support is conditional on whether government is delivering equitable services, economic opportunity, and neighborhood investment, and it can be withdrawn or demobilized if the representative loses credibility as an advocate for the district's material interests. A representative who campaigns as though the seat is permanently secure will eventually discover that it is not." },
          { name: "Ignoring the District's Renter Constituency", tag: "avoid", why: "At 26.8% renters, GA-HD-91 has nearly three in ten households without homeownership — a population with direct economic interests in housing affordability, tenant protection, and equitable access to homeownership that often diverge from homeowner priorities. Legislation that benefits homeowners at renters' expense, or that treats housing as a secondary issue, will gradually mobilize a constituency that is large enough to swing a future competitive election. A representative who cannot articulate a concrete vision for housing equity across both homeowner and renter populations is leaving a latent opposition constituency unaddressed." }
