          "Engage the district's 26.8% renter constituency with concrete housing policy: affordable housing development, tenant protections, and equitable access to homeownership are the economic security issues for renters in a metro Atlanta district where housing costs are rising faster than $70k incomes.",
          "Build accountability relationships with neighborhood institutions — Black churches, civic associations, schools — that can surface constituent concerns directly rather than relying on electoral pressure to identify problems; in a safe seat, these relationships are the early warning system for governance drift.",
          "Do not assume that 63% Black voting support is permanent or inherited: it is conditional on visible delivery on education quality, public safety, infrastructure maintenance, and economic opportunity for young adults, all of which are measurable and will be evaluated by constituents whether the next election is contested or not."
