        "Build proactive Spanish-language constituent service for the 10.49% Hispanic community: in a Black-majority district, the Latino constituency can easily become invisible—but at one-in-ten residents, they are large enough that organized engagement or organized opposition can shift competitive dynamics; proactive investment in bilingual service and economic mobility support creates cross-ethnic loyalty unavailable to challengers.",
        "Develop workforce development and vocational training agenda for the 63.8% non-college-attainment majority: at $86,234 income, many households have achieved stability through skilled trades, entrepreneurship, and career advancement without four-year degrees, and their economic concerns around credential pathways, small-business support, and workforce training are materially different from professional-class priorities.",
        "Treat the unopposed 2024 result as a mandate to build community infrastructure rather than a signal that no further investment is needed: in a safe Democratic district, the only viable threat is a primary challenger who runs on active community engagement—the best protection against this is visible, specific legislative delivery on homeowner, healthcare, and school quality priorities."
