          { name: "Treating 2024 Unopposed Status as Proof of Electoral Safety", tag: "avoid", why: "The absence of Republican opposition in 2024 is not evidence of a safely Democratic district — it is evidence that Republicans have not yet targeted this seat. A plurality-minority district with 61% renters, $63,482 income, and no established incumbent reputation in every demographic community is plausibly competitive if a Republican recognizes it as a pickup opportunity and invests accordingly. Treating the unopposed result as proof of invulnerability, rather than as a window to build infrastructure before competition arrives, is a strategic error that will become visible in 2026 or 2028." },
          { name: "Assuming Demographic Diversity Alone Produces Democratic Turnout", tag: "avoid", why: "HD-96 is demographically diverse but not necessarily polarized along educational or ideological lines in the way some suburban districts are. The 32.7 median age, 61% renter rate, and $63,482 income suggest a working-family constituency that evaluates representatives on concrete results — housing affordability, education quality, job availability — rather than on partisan culture-war positioning. Representing this district effectively requires specific accomplishment on material concerns, not rhetorical alignment with Democratic base priorities on issues unrelated to constituent economic security." }
