          "Invest visibly in representation and leadership pipeline development across minority communities; at 61.4% combined, Hispanic, Black, and Asian residents are the demographic majority but require active engagement to remain convinced the representative is advancing their distinct interests and not absorbing them into an abstract Democratic coalition.",
          "Address housing affordability specifically for the renter-majority and younger professional constituencies: the 24.5% renter rate and 35.6-year median age signal a constituency where housing cost burden and access to ownership pathways are direct quality-of-life and economic mobility concerns that shape vote choice.",
          "Treat the 28% Republican opposition not as the primary threat—it is not—but as a signal of where constituent service gaps or perception problems exist; the supermajority is durable only if all four major constituencies (educated professionals, Hispanic, Black, Asian) remain convinced that active Democratic governance serves their interests better than any alternative."
