          "Recognize that 61% is not a durable majority: the combination of high education, young median age, and significant renter population makes this a persuadable district where Democratic opposition at 39% signals active dissatisfaction rather than baseline partisan distribution. Any incumbent who campaigns as though 61% is secure rather than fragile will be vulnerable to a credible challenger who organizes the swing constituencies actively."
