          "Avoid the complacency trap: unopposed races often precede primary challenges or sudden Republican recruitment of a credible local candidate; use the electoral safety to build constituent relationships and policy record that would survive a competitive challenge, rather than assuming the opposition will remain absent.",
          "Engage the 27.4% college-educated constituency on education funding and workforce development: this subconstituency is the most likely swing group if dissatisfied with education policy or school resource allocation, and specific attention to school quality and student outcomes is the surest way to retain them.",
          "Recognize the 33.75% white population as a potential swing constituency: in a Black-majority district where Democrats are unopposed, white working-class voters are most likely to be persuadable by Republican recruitment; addressing white working-class economic concerns alongside Black constituent priorities is the best way to prevent future Republican competitive entry."
