          "Engage the Black constituency actively and authentically: at 28.88%, this is the largest minority population in the district and represents nearly three in ten residents; governance that does not include deliberate engagement with Black community institutions, economic concerns, and leadership is leaving substantial constituent needs unaddressed and creating political space for opposition mobilization.",
          "Do not assume 68% insulates against economic messaging: a 32% Democratic opposition floor in a working-class district with renter populations and below-median income is a baseline that can shift if voters perceive the incumbent as indifferent to their economic struggles; active constituent service and visible delivery on kitchen-table issues is necessary to hold this seat against a credible challenger.",
          "Build a durable economic coalition that includes both homeowners and renters: at 27.1% renters and majority homeownership with modest income, this district contains two constituencies with overlapping but distinct economic interests; messaging that addresses both housing affordability and property tax fairness, and both healthcare access and wage growth, reaches the whole district rather than just its Republican base."
