          { name: "Defaulting to Abstract Conservative Ideology Without Addressing Material Constituent Concerns", tag: "avoid", why: "A $96,875 affluent, 38.1% college-educated, 36.8-year-old constituency with 75.8% renters evaluates candidates on concrete delivery — school quality, housing affordability, property tax fairness, economic opportunity — not partisan doctrine. Any candidate who campaigns on ideology rather than constituent service and competence will lose the college-educated swing voters and minority voters who are swing constituencies in this district; in an unopposed race, this vulnerability remained invisible, but it is real." }
