          "Lead on working-class economic security: the 36% renter rate and $48,218 median income signal constituents under real financial pressure for whom housing affordability, wage policy, and healthcare access are direct quality-of-life issues. Specific legislative accomplishments on rental assistance, minimum wage, or healthcare expansion demonstrate concrete delivery rather than abstract messaging.",
          "Build authentic relationships with Black, white, and Hispanic communities separately and simultaneously: a 42.45%-45.23% Black-white split with 7.83% Hispanic requires constituent attention that does not treat all three as interchangeable. Understand each community's specific economic concerns—employment pathways, housing discrimination, agricultural policy—and offer concrete answers tailored to each.",
          "Identify and address what might activate Republican opposition in 2026: whether economic anxiety, frustration with incumbent service responsiveness, or specific policy disagreement, understanding the potential opposition's basis before it coalesces allows proactive messaging and constituent relationship-building that prevents a credible challenger from gaining traction."
