          "Engage the 23.1% college-educated constituency deliberately: teachers, healthcare workers, and public-sector professionals who drive community institutions deserve specific attention to education funding, public-sector compensation, and healthcare policy rather than assuming they are subsumed into the broader majority-race narrative.",
          "Treat the 33% opposition as a diagnostic indicator, not a static fact: understand whether opposition is concentrated among the white 22.56% and Hispanic 3.51% communities with specific grievances around service delivery, among voters frustrated by the pace of housing improvement, or both — and address those concerns directly rather than assuming they will not grow.",
          "Do not campaign a 67% margin as a safe supermajority: the combination of high renter concentration, constrained median income, and material economic pressure means this district's voters evaluate on delivery, not inheritance; any incumbent who consolidates the existing base without demonstrating concrete improvement in cost-of-living metrics risks erosion in the next cycle."
