          "Build explicit constituent attention to educational access and workforce development: at 16.3% college attainment, HD-155's young adults face real constraints on economic mobility. Community college funding, apprenticeship programs, and the pathway from education to stable employment are high-salience issues for working-class families evaluating whether state government is investing in their children's futures.",
          "Monitor African American voter engagement and satisfaction continuously: the 36.84% Black population is the largest single demographic group, and their turnout and candidate preference in any competitive cycle would determine the seat's outcome. Regular, specific constituent feedback from Black churches, civic organizations, and community leaders should be part of baseline constituent stewardship, not just campaign-season activity.",
          "Avoid any legislative record or rhetoric that dismisses economic hardship or positions working-class renter and minority concerns as special-interest advocacy rather than constituent service; in a district where one-third of households rent and median income is barely above $50,000, the material struggles of working families are the default political terrain."
