          { name: "Ceding the Black Community Entirely to Opposition Organizing", tag: "avoid", why: "Allowing the 30% Black population to remain disengaged and available for opposition mobilization around economic issues—particularly in a district where Black and white working-class households share material concerns—is a strategic failure. Even if partisan alignment remains unchanged, a representative who builds visible constituent relationships with the Black community improves governance quality, increases margin security, and prevents the opposition from organizing this constituency around legitimate economic grievances." }
