          "Lead any challenge or defense with a concrete economic security agenda: wage floor policy, healthcare cost management, rental market fairness, and workforce development are material concerns for a $52,561-median-income, 34.9%-renter, 13.7%-college-educated constituency, not abstract partisan messaging.",
          "Build explicit racial coalition governance — the near-parity white (50.55%) and Black (40.12%) split means any winning candidate must articulate a specific vision for economic fairness and equitable service delivery that resonates across both communities simultaneously rather than treating them as separate constituencies.",
          "Address the college-attainment gap (13.7%) directly: either with a workforce-development agenda that does not require four-year degrees, or with a specific plan to make higher education and vocational training accessible to young adults in the district — otherwise younger adults remain economically trapped regardless of how they vote."
