          "Build explicit Hispanic community relationships; at 6.3% but growing, the Hispanic population is small enough to be invisible in a heavily white district but large enough that active engagement demonstrates inclusive governance and prevents future demographic-driven competition.",
          "Do not assume the 28% opposition is inert; it represents college-educated professionals, public employees, and younger renters whose economic interests may align with Republican governance but whose fiscal and social priorities differ — specific constituent service to this group prevents it from mobilizing around a challenger."
