          { name: "Overlooking the District's Working-Class Character in Favor of Progressive Symbolic Politics", tag: "avoid", why: "With 28.2% college attainment, 35.8% renters, and $69,426 median household income, GA-SD-4 is a working-class district where material economic concerns outweigh cultural or identity-based messaging. A legislative agenda centered on abstract progressive priorities while overlooking concrete solutions to housing costs, childcare affordability, or job quality will leave the incumbent vulnerable to a challenger—of any party—who frames the agenda around what working families actually need. The district's composition demands that representation focus on economic security and opportunity, not on positioning the representative as ideologically progressive." }
