          { name: "Assuming 55% Is a Durable Partisan Majority", tag: "avoid", why: "The 55% result reflects conditional support from college-educated swing voters, not locked-in Democratic partisanship in a district where nearly half the electorate chose the opposition and economic evaluations are primary. Any incumbent or challenger who campaigns as though 55% is a stable floor rather than a working margin held together by specific deliverables on school quality, healthcare access, and cost management will find that margin eroded by a credible alternative. This is a performance-based seat, not a partisan one; messaging must lead with measurable outcomes, not party affiliation." }
