          "Manage the demographic diversity as a strength, not a coalition to be managed: with no group above 35%, success requires specific, evidence-based engagement with each community's particular concerns — Asian American healthcare access and economic mobility, Black community school investment and criminal justice outcomes, Hispanic economic mobility and education pathways, and white professional households on fiscal management and service delivery.",
          "Treat 55% as a working margin, not a safe hold: in a district this diverse and educated, with nearly 40% renters and professional workers who evaluate on performance, any incumbent or challenger who assumes the current 45-55 split is durable is strategically vulnerable; sustained engagement and documented results on the three core issues (schools, healthcare, infrastructure) are necessary conditions for winning re-election, not optional enhancements."
