          "Lead with education quality and K-12 funding: at 36.7-year median age with school-age children and $89,926 income, families in this district are directly invested in public school performance and teacher compensation as both quality-of-life and economic-mobility issues; specific legislative achievements on education funding are more persuasive than general rhetoric.",
          "Address housing affordability directly for the 23.6% renter population: at $89,926 median income, many households are cost-burdened by rent, and younger adults are evaluating whether they can afford to stay in the district or form households here; this is not a footnote, but a material economic concern affecting family formation and household economics.",
          "Build healthcare access and affordability into the base message: at $89,926 income, families are above poverty but often underinsured; healthcare costs are a concrete squeeze on household budgets even at this income level, and candidates who speak to this pressure with specific policy solutions (Medicaid sustainability, prescription drug costs, ACA protections) build credibility across demographic lines."
