          "Address educational credential attainment and workforce development explicitly: at 21.3% college-educated, the district has the lowest educational attainment signal in the dataset; partner with community colleges, employer networks, and workforce development agencies to create visible pathways from high school into credentials that lead to wage growth and economic mobility.",
          "Prevent the emergence of an alternative by establishing visible, material economic impact: unopposed incumbents who vanish between elections are vulnerable; a candidate who can point to specific small business support, job training completions, housing units created, or employer investments attracted during their tenure builds the political durability that comes from constituency members perceiving direct benefit."
