          "Recognize that 73% in a district with one-third non-white population is not a structural supermajority: if demographic shifts or minority voter mobilization increase opposition among Asian, Hispanic, or Black residents, or if younger professionals drift toward Democratic candidates on specific issues, this margin compresses rapidly — treat it as a working margin that requires active constituent engagement, not a permanent coalition."
