        "Lead on housing affordability and economic mobility as the shared material interest of the majority-minority constituency: $75,356 median income with 38.9% renter rate describes a working-to-middle-class family constituency where housing costs, childcare, and healthcare premiums are real budget constraints that both Black and Hispanic families face together.",
        "Invest in year-round constituent engagement infrastructure rather than campaign-cycle activation: at 35.3-year median age with 38.9% renters, this constituency is vulnerable to turnout volatility in lower-salience elections; authentic relationships built through ongoing constituent service and community presence sustain turnout levels that the unopposed presidential-cycle result may make seem automatic.",
        "Do not treat the 25.25% white population as irrelevant to the Democratic coalition: even in a 70%+ minority district, white residents who have chosen to live in a majority-minority community may be natural allies on economic and community development issues, and specific constituent attention builds a broader coalition and prevents a future challenger from mobilizing white opposition."
