          { name: "Assuming Unopposed Status Guarantees Electoral Safety", tag: "avoid", why: "A 100% win in 2024 with no Republican opponent reflects current partisan dominance but provides no protection against a primary challenger or a credible general opponent who offers a different vision of economic representation. Unopposed victories often mask internal vulnerabilities around constituent service, legislative effectiveness, or authentic connection to the constituency's economic priorities. Treating the 100% result as evidence of durable incumbency advantage rather than as a baseline to be defended and improved upon creates vulnerability to a challenger who demonstrates real economic delivery." },
          { name: "Prioritizing Abstract Progressive Positioning Over Material Economic Delivery", tag: "avoid", why: "For a working-class constituency at $70,980 median income with 34.9% renting and limited college attainment, abstract policy positioning or rhetorical commitment to progressive values is a weak substitute for concrete legislative results on housing, wages, and economic opportunity. A representative who delivers tangible improvements in the constituency's economic security builds durable political power; one who emphasizes ideological positioning over material improvement creates space for a challenger who promises real economic delivery. This constituency will hold an incumbent accountable for whether their economic position is actually improving." }
