          "Build a legislative record on job quality and wage growth, not just employment numbers: the $70,980 median masks households below that threshold working multiple jobs with inadequate benefits. Policies on minimum wage, worker organizing, childcare costs, and healthcare access determine whether working families' incomes actually improve or stagnate — and whether they perceive their representative as fighting for their economic security.",
