          "Treat unopposed status as opportunity, not guarantee: a Black-majority urban district with genuine economic constraints can generate primary challenge from candidates who credibly promise more aggressive governance; consolidate the incumbent coalition through concrete delivery on housing, education, and healthcare rather than assuming 100% translates to secure reelection.",
          "Engage the renter constituency with specificity: at 34.7% renter rate, housing policy — tenant protection, eviction prevention, rental assistance, development of affordable housing stock — is a direct constituent service and political organizing opportunity; state senators who move legislation and secure resources for renter households build durable urban coalitions.",
          "Build K-12 education as the signature issue: at 28.1% college attainment and 35.8 median age, parenting and school quality are central to household economic decision-making; a senator who secures funding increases for district schools, addresses teacher compensation, and expands early childhood access translates education commitment into visible constituency benefit."
