          "Lead on education funding and public safety outcomes: the college-educated, high-income constituency has children in or connected to public schools and lives in suburban communities where they expect demonstrable public safety results; specific accomplishments and measurable metrics on school funding increases and crime reduction are the currency that builds durability with this demographic.",
          "Engage the renter population (21.7%) and younger professionals (37.7-year median age) with concrete housing and economic opportunity messaging: this constituency is mobile and not bound by generational partisan loyalty; they evaluate based on whether state policy is addressing their actual constraints around housing affordability, student loan management, and economic mobility.",
          "Build distributed constituent relationships across the district's four major demographic communities—white, Black, Hispanic, and Asian—rather than assuming Democratic partisanship consolidates them; each community has distinct economic concerns (school quality for families, workforce access for working-class communities, small business support for immigrant communities) that require specific, evidence-based policy response."
