          "Do not take the 35.9% renter constituency for granted: engage young professionals, educated minorities, and renters with specific policy positions on housing affordability, student debt, and healthcare access — not as Democratic appeals, but as credible conservative governance that addresses their material constraints without abandoning the homeowner majority.",
          "Map the 13.2% demographic gap and build constituent relationships accordingly: understand whether this population is concentrated geographically, whether it skews younger or older, and whether it is primarily Hispanic, Asian, or other — then develop targeted engagement strategies that prevent this constituency from becoming the organizing target of a sophisticated Democratic challenger.",
          "Monitor the gap between the 37% opposition and the 35.9% renter rate for strategic signals: if Democratic performance is significantly outperforming the renter percentage, it indicates persuasion momentum among this educated, persuadable constituency that requires immediate constituent engagement and messaging adjustment."
